@page "/orders/print-station"

@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]
@layout EtsyShopManager.Web.Components.Layout.AccountLayout
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@* Static SSR page left open on a PC by the printer: print-station.js asks the app for queued packing slips every few
   seconds (AutoPrintService.ClaimAsync), prints them in a hidden frame with the same printout as Orders → Print packing
   slips, and reports them printed. Started with the browser's silent-print switch, nothing needs clicking. *@
<PageTitle>Print station · Etsy Shop Manager</PageTitle>

<h1>Print station</h1>

<p id="ps-status" class="print-station-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Starting…</p>

<p class="muted">
    Leave this page open on a computer that can print. It checks for packing slips every 10 seconds and prints them
    on this computer's default printer, then marks them printed. Slips queued while it's closed print when it opens again.
</p>

<p>
    <button type="button" id="ps-test" class="btn">Print a test page</button>
</p>

<h2 class="print-station-heading">Printed here</h2>
<ul id="ps-log" class="print-station-log">
    <li class="muted">Nothing yet.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="print-station-heading">Printing without a dialog</h2>
<p class="muted">
    Browsers show a print dialog unless they are started with silent printing. Open the station with this command (Chrome
    takes the same switches; the separate profile keeps it apart from other Edge windows), and make the slip printer
    Windows' default printer:
</p>
<code class="print-station-command">msedge --kiosk-printing --user-data-dir=%LOCALAPPDATA%\EsmPrintStation --app=@(Nav.BaseUri)orders/print-station</code>
<p class="muted">
    Put that command in a shortcut in the Startup folder to open the station whenever the computer signs in.
</p>

<script src="print-station.js"></script>
